  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Operational and Tactical Interdiction Capabilities  of Georgia Border Police</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project, financed by Export Control and Related Border Security (EXBS), and implemented by the International Organization for Migration (IOM) Mission to Georgia, aims at strengthening coherent border-security oriented skills of Ministry of Internal Affairs (MIA) officials responsible for the surveillance of the green border of Georgia. Within MIA responsibilities, the Border Police is tasked with operating and responding to increasing cross-border challenges. This project is designed to provide tailored interventions for the benefit of the Border Police personnel, to enhance their capacities and skills according to the latest best international standards for border guarding, response operations, intelligence collection, investigation, and risk analysis. More specifically, the Action entails a series of trainings on Command and Control, Border Surveillance Techniques and Tactics, Risk Analysis, Investigation and Intelligence. The Georgian Border Police authorities will also benefit from a study visit to a European Union Member State Border, to enhance their technical and practical knowledge on the realities they face and the measures taken to respond to cross-border crimes. The project will be implemented during a period of 18 months.</narrative>
  </description>
